<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">17062026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>The United States and Iran have signed an accord on the Strait of Hormuz... and Israel's Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu wasn't told it was coming.</s>
<s>After three months of Israeli strikes meant to break Iran, it's Tehran that kept its grip on the world's most important oil chokepoint, while Trump publicly called the parallel Lebanon campaign deadly.</s>
<s>Netanyahu now heads into elections with southern Lebanon still under bombardment and his closest ally negotiating over his head.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>In Myanmar, the people who survive landmine blasts lose their limbs first, and then their livelihoods.</s>
<s>Both the military junta and the resistance forces sowing the country's farmland keep laying mines, and in a collapsed economy survivors find no prosthetics, no rehabilitation, and no way to earn.</s>
<s>With no peace talks scheduled, the war's casualties keep accruing long after the world's attention has moved on.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A British public inquiry into alleged war crimes has agreed to hide the identities of two senior <sub alias="S A S">SAS</sub> commanders who led units during killings in Afghanistan between twenty-ten and twenty-thirteen.</s>
<s>The inquiry's chair accepted a national-security argument, the same mechanism by which institutional power shields its own decision-makers even inside a war-crimes hearing.</s>
<s>He may revisit the anonymity orders once the inquiry ends, though no timeline has been set, and Afghan families wait to learn who commanded the men accused.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A Russian satirist who caricatured Vladimir Putin and Belarus's Lukashenko has been shot dead in eastern Poland, metres from a Belarusian consulate.</s>
<s>Semyon Skrepetsky was hit five times, and two Belarusian nationals were detained nearby, in a killing that shows transnational repression reaching deep into the European Union.</s>
<s>The gunman remains at large, and for Russia's exiles abroad, distance is no longer safety.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>SpaceX has agreed to buy the artificial-intelligence coding tool Cursor in an all-stock deal worth sixty billion dollars.</s>
<s>Struck just days after the company's public listing and months after it absorbed Musk's xAI, the purchase turns a launch firm into a full AI conglomerate, and a developer's daily coding tool into a strategic asset inside one man's empire.</s>
<s>The deal's set to close in the third quarter, and for the engineers who depend on these tools, the concentration of power is the story.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The Bank of Japan has raised its benchmark interest rate to one percent, the first time it's reached that level since nineteen ninety-five.</s>
<s>Japan imports ninety-five percent of its crude from the Middle East, and war-driven energy inflation has spread through its supply chains, pushing wholesale prices up six percent in May.</s>
<s>The bank's pledged further hikes if inflation persists, ending a generation of near-zero money.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India's power grid hit two hundred seventy gigawatts of demand last month, and air conditioning alone now accounts for a quarter of that peak.</s>
<s>Analysts found that nudging fifteen million new buyers from two-star to five-star units would save seven hundred twenty-four million dollars a year.</s>
<s>Without sustained efficiency gains, power shortages are projected as early as twenty-twenty-eight.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>China's Belt and Road energy investment reached almost ninety-four billion dollars last year, with oil-and-gas deals tripling to seventy-one and a half billion.</s>
<s>Megadeals in Nigeria and Congo drove sixty percent of that gain, and Chinese firms retain control of the supply chains they build.</s>
<s>Even as the world talks of transition, Beijing is locking in the fossil-fuel infrastructure of the Global South for decades.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Frozen rubbish heaps in Greenland have preserved four and a half thousand years of human history, intact.</s>
<s>Permafrost has held the bones, shells, and waste of Paleo-Inuit, Norse Vikings, and Danish settlers as a high-resolution archive of how each culture fed itself, an archive that decay has destroyed everywhere warmer.</s>
<s>As the Arctic thaws, the very ice that protected this record is now erasing it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In South Africa, a woman named Nokuthula Mguni died after a Johannesburg hospital demanded payment upfront before treating her.</s>
<s>South African law bars charging for emergency care, but staff at Charlotte Maxeke told the Zimbabwean permit-holder that all foreigners must pay first.</s>
<s>The provincial health department hasn't responded, and a law written to protect the vulnerable proved no protection at the door.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Researchers in Italy say autism isn't one brain pattern but two, biologically distinct and opposite.</s>
<s>Functional scans of nine hundred forty autistic people revealed connectivity that was either unusually weak or unusually strong, each tied to its own genetic mechanism.</s>
<s>Yet fifty-nine percent of participants fit neither type, a reminder of how much of the brain we still can't map.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Chemists have built a water-splitting catalyst that runs for a thousand hours without breaking down.</s>
<s>Anchored ruthenium atoms offload oxidative charge to a metal-oxide host, preventing the dissolution that normally destroys the most efficient catalysts within hours, and it uses eighty percent less precious metal than today's standard.</s>
<s>Durability, not just efficiency, is the gate on cheap green hydrogen, and commercial validation is the next test.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Authorities in Russian-occupied Crimea have banned motorcycles and mopeds overnight, because their engines sound like incoming drones.</s>
<s>Air-defence crews rely on cheap acoustic sensors to detect attacks, and that detection layer is so fragile that ordinary traffic noise degrades it, as Ukraine intensifies its strikes on the peninsula.</s>
<s>A five-hundred-dollar drone has now forced a curfew on an entire region's roads.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>France's domestic intelligence agency will drop the American firm Palantir and switch to the French company ChapsVision.</s>
<s>Germany's own security service made the same choice last month, both citing mistrust of Palantir's ties to the United States.</s>
<s>Palantir insists its contract remains fully in force, but Europe's appetite for digital sovereignty is plainly growing.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>For the first time, most of Spotify's listeners are streaming music in languages other than English.</s>
<s>AI-driven localization and cheaper tiered pricing across Africa, Asia, and Latin America have shifted the platform's centre of gravity away from its English-speaking core.</s>
<s>The company still won't disclose what it pays per stream in those new markets, where the growth is now happening.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>